  <p>
    <strong>Digital currency markets have shed billions once again, as the entire crypto-economy has been cut down from well over $2 trillion to today’s $1.44 trillion market valuation. Bitcoin was coasting along just above the $38k handle before 9 p.m. (EST) yesterday evening but after that point, sellers started capitulating and the price dropped under $34k. </strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Crypto Economy Shaves Billions
  </h2>
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      Crypto prices are down on Sunday after a number of markets tried to regain strength on Friday and Saturday. Bitcoin (BTC) and a number of other digital assets have lost significant value, as last week’s crypto market losses were some of the biggest in history.
    </li>
    <li>
      On Sunday, bitcoin (BTC) is trading for $35,385 per unit and is down 7% today and down 23% during the last seven days.
    </li>
  </ul><figure id="attachment_461164" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-461164" style="width: 2416px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-461164 size-full" title="Crypto Markets Lose Billions, Weak Hands Capitulate, Stablecoin Market Surpasses $100 Billion" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53.jpg" alt="Crypto Markets Lose Billions, Weak Hands Capitulate, Stablecoin Market Surpasses $100 Billion" width="2416" height="1316" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53.jpg 2416w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53-300x163.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53-1024x558.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53-768x418.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53-1536x837.jpg 1536w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53-2048x1116.jpg 2048w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53-696x379.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53-1392x758.jpg 1392w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53-1068x582.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53-771x420.jpg 771w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/bitstamp_btc_usd-sun_23_may_07_36_53-1920x1046.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2416px) 100vw, 2416px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-461164" class="wp-caption-text">BTC/USD on Sunday morning at 8:00 a.m. Eastern Standard Time (May 23, 2021).</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      BTC dominance has increased since dropping to a low of 40%. Sunday’s stats show BTC dominance is 45.9%, while ethereum (ETH) captures 17.3%.
    </li>
    <li>
      The second-largest crypto asset, ethereum (ETH), is down over 11% today and down 39% for the week.
    </li>
  </ul><figure id="attachment_461163" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-461163" style="width: 2416px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-461163 size-full" title="Crypto Markets Lose Billions, Weak Hands Capitulate, Stablecoin Market Surpasses $100 Billion" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04.jpg" alt="Crypto Markets Lose Billions, Weak Hands Capitulate, Stablecoin Market Surpasses $100 Billion" width="2416" height="1316" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04.jpg 2416w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04-300x163.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04-1024x558.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04-768x418.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04-1536x837.jpg 1536w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04-2048x1116.jpg 2048w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04-696x379.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04-1392x758.jpg 1392w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04-1068x582.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04-771x420.jpg 771w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/deribit_eth_usd-sun_23_may_07_37_04-1920x1046.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2416px) 100vw, 2416px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-461163" class="wp-caption-text">ETH/USD on Sunday morning at 8:00 a.m. Eastern Standard Time (May 23, 2021).</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <ul>
    <li>
      Out of the top ten crypto assets, the two biggest losers include binance coin (BNB) which shed 53% during the last week and polkadot (DOT), which dropped 53.82% during the last seven days.
    </li>
    <li>
      On the other hand, the top ten digital coins that saw the least amount of losses last week include bitcoin (BTC) and dogecoin (DOGE).
    </li>
  </ul>
  
  <p>
